WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.720
Phineas and Ferb have some serious problems with realism.

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:05.260
And no, I'm not talking about secret agent platypuses,

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:07.560
evil scientists with endless supplies of money,

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:10.740
or the fact that two elementary-school-aged brothers have managed to travel to space

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:14.480
with machines assembled from materials purchased at Home Depot!

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:14.980
NO!

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:17.920
I'm talking about the opening of the show!

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.080
(Nostalgia Plays) ♫ There's a hundred and four days of summer vacation-

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:25.660
A hundred and four days of summer vacation? On what planet?

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.900
My elementary school only allowed 88 days of summer vacation!

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.360
I checked the calendars of a bunch of other school districts,

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.380
and the longest summer break I could find was 90!

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.455
Not only do Phineas and Ferb have a slew of

00:00:36.455 --> 00:00:39.155
cool inventions, unlimited budget for their summer shenanigans,

00:00:39.155 --> 00:00:42.015
and a cool secret agent pet, but they get an

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:44.780
extra 16 days of summer vacation?!

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:47.780
THAT, my friends, is a bridge too far.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:53.220
"This summer just keeps going on and on, it feels like it's been going on for like, 4 years."

00:00:53.480 --> 00:01:10.140
*Film Theory intro*

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:13.200
Hello internet! Welcome to Film Theory!

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:17.220
The show where I put the summer vacations of fictional cartoon characters under the microscope.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:21.560
Because my own summer vacations were mostly spent watching fictional cartoon characters.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:22.820
And the Price Is Right!

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:24.500
*The Price is Right audio*

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.000
Today I'm talking about Phineas and Ferb,

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.980
which just last week celebrated the 10th anniversary

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:30.040
since their debut.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:31.660
Now I can already hear some of you saying,

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:34.080
"Matpat, aren't you a little old to be watching a

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:35.560
10-year old Disney channel cartoon?"

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.700
Yes... ... ... (Yes I am)

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:39.860
On it's face, Phineas and Ferb may seem like a formulaic

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.860
kids show but what's so brilliant about it

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:42.920
is that's the whole point.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:47.180
Unlike some cartoons which slowly grow repetitive over years of syndication.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.260
Phineas and Ferb intentionally started out as a fomulaic show

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:54.380
and it keeps things fresh  by constantly finding was to subvert its own cliches.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.120
Most episodes follow the same basic formula

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:00.280
So for those of you who aren't familiar with the show, I'll take you through a typical episode

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:05.000
Two brothers, the chatty up-beat Phineas and the silent stoic Ferb are on summer vacation

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.560
And they're looking for a fresh and exciting way to spend the day

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.420
The neighbor girl Isabella walks by to ask

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:10.660
Isabella: "Whatcha doin?"

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:13.520
And something happens to give Phineas the inspiration to say

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:14.580
Phineas: "I know what we're gonna do today!"

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:19.000
Someone then takes notice of the fact that their pet Perry the platypus is gone missing and says.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.340
Phineas: "Hey, where's Perry?"

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:24.680
The episode then splits onto and A story, which follows the boys and their inventive shenanigans.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:27.960
And a B story that follows the secret life of Perry the Platypus.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:36.300
Who dons a brown fedora as he goes to thwart the latest invention of the villainous Dr. Heinz Doofenshmirtz, a local mad scientist.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.720
Doofenshmirtz: "I'm an evil scientist not a mad scientist. T-There's a difference"

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.300
Dr. Doofenshmirtz is always cooking up a new invention

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.080
Like the Drill-inator

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.280
The Ugly-inator

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.200
Or the Gloom-inator 3000-inator

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:50.460
Generally something with a name that ends in inator and has to be stopped. Figured you'd see the pattern...

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:55.680
Several story beats later the boys have their fun, Perry the Platypus defeats Dr. Doofenshmirtz's latest scheme.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:00.680
And in the process of beating the evil scientist, something happens that destroys whatever the boys were working on all day

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:04.240
Eliminating all evidence of their shenanigans before their parents come home,

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:07.680
wiping the slate clean for them to come up with some new invention tomorrow.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:10.400
The defeated Dr. Doofenshmirtz yells into the wind

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.340
Doofenshmirtz: "CURSE YOU PERRY THE PLATYPUS!!!!"

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:14.280
Perry goes back home to the boys

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:15.920
Phineas: "Oh, there you are Perry."

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:19.620
And the boys check another day of summer vacation off the calendar

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.580
Now, even though I'm talking about Phineas and Ferb the TV show,

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:25.780
I'm not actually gonna be talking about Phineas and Ferb the brothers.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:28.940
Instead I wanna focus today's episode on the villain of the story

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:31.920
Dr. Heniz Doofenshmirtz, creator and sole member of

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:36.040
♫ Doofenshmirtz Evil Incorporated! ♫

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:39.900
Specifically I'm interested in one very important question here

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:43.720
Why hasn't this obviously evil villain ever been arrested?

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:46.980
I mean, it's not like there aren't people and Animals trying to stop him.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:52.540
Perry the platypus is an agent of the Organization Without a Cool Acronym, or OWCA for short.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:54.620
Doofenshmirtz: "Man, these guys are really bad at acronyming."

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:58.280
And most days, his sole purpose is to track down the despicable doc.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:01.980
And clearly Doofenshmirtz is guilty of breaking more then a few laws.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:07.740
Grand Larceny from time he stole all the city's Mr. Slushie Burger statues in "Does this duckbill make me look fat?"

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:14.460
And the time he some how managed to steal all the steaks in the Tri-stake ar- sorry the Tri-state area in "Comet Kermillian."

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:19.540
Not to mention his mistreatment of Animals like the time he enslaved monkeys to work in his volcano laundromat.

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:25.400
Given the fact that the OWCA employs animals, I would think that they would be taking that one pretty personally

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:28.780
We also know that the OWCA could arrest him if they wanted to

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:34.440
In the episode "Oh there you are, Perry." We see Perry take on a more serious villain, the Regurgitatior..

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.140
You just can't keep him down....

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:40.400
At the end of the episode, we learn the the Regurgitator has been apprehended and put into prison.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:44.820
Major Francis Monogram: "You've defeated the Regurgitator, as a matter of fact, he just landed in our prison."

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:48.440
Notice that Perry's boss, Major Monogram, says "Our prison."

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:52.480
This is an OWCA holding facility, not some generic state prison.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:55.180
They don't even have the excuse of not being able to find him.

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:59.120
He has an enormous building in the middle of the city with a giant freaking name on the front!

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:03.560
In short, if the OWCA wanted to arrest Doofenshmirtz, they could...

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:04.760
But they don't!

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:06.260
They don't even try!

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:09.500
Which means, something else has to be going on here...

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.700
Something a bit more devious and under handed

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:14.700
And that is what we're gonna expose today

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:19.500
Our first clues lie in the Phineas and Ferb special: "The OWCA Files."

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:23.280
Heinz Doofenshmirtz was once part of the agent training program at OWCA

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:28.740
Which is a weird quirk of his past considering that the organization only allows animals to serve as agents.

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:33.280
Major Francis Monogram: "Ya know Karl it's weird that he's not an animal. We should fire him."

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:34.740
Karl: "I am already on it Sir."

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:40.740
Doofenshmirtz though, found a loophole, he's legally considered an ocelot due to being raised by wild animals.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:43.340
Meaning that he was lucky enough to get into the program.

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:50.340
Doofenshmirtz: "I would say that's probably the first time anyone has described my being abandoned by my parents and raised by central american wildcats as lucky."

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:53.740
Why Doofenshmirtz left the agent training program though is a mystery.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:56.200
But it seems like he was fired due to incompetence.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.700
We see throughout the series that Doof is good at building things....

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:01.900
He's just not good at using the things he builds...

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:04.880
Major Monogram even says it himself in episode "Agent Doof"

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:08.400
Major Monogram: "You've done more harm inside the agency then ever you did outside."

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:13.580
In short, OWCA doesn't want Doofenshmirtz as a member of their organization due to his distructive tendacies.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.760
Major Monogram: "Doofenshmirtz!"

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:19.540
But thanks to a few select details in the Phineas and Ferb movie,

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:22.900
We know that they weren't ready to get rid of him completely.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:31.040
In the movie Phineas and Ferb, Across the 2nd Dimension, Perry the Platypys has to break OWCA protocol and reveal his secret identity to the two brothers.

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:35.380
Which, according to regulations means that he has to be relocated to a new host family.

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:39.700
Major Monogram: "Now that Agent P's cover has been blown, you wont be allowed to see him anymore."

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:42.340
However, Major Monogram comes up with an alternate solution

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:42.720
However, Major Monogram comes up with an alternate solution.

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:46.360
They can use the amnesia-inator to wipe Phineas and Ferbs memories,

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:46.300
They can use the Amnesia-inator to wipe Phineas and Ferb's memories,

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.920
Allowing Perry to continue to live with them as an undercover agent

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:49.940
Allowing Perry to continue to live with them as an undercover agent

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:52.300
Isabella: "So none of us will remember  any of today?"

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:52.300
Isabella: "So none of us will remember  any of today?"

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:52.960
Major Monogram: "That's right."

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:53.060
Major Monogram: "That's right."

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:58.500
The boys agree, and in the process the lose all the memories of the adventures that they has while visiting the second dimension with Perry

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:02.220
But! Hold on for a second there, Amnesia-inator?

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:05.980
That sounds like the sorta stupid name that Dr. Doofenshmirtz would give an invention.

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:07.720
And indeed it is...

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:10.340
Karl: "Dr. Doofenshmirtz's Amnesia-inator."

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:14.740
We find out in the movie that Perry's brown isn't just for fashion....

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:21.680
Hidden in his hat is an auto-scan replication device. Which OWCA has been using to gather data on all of Doof's inventions,

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:24.660
So that they can then replicate them  of themselves

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:28.960
Major Monogram: "Every operative is equipped with an auto-scan replication device, just like the one in your hat,"

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:33.980
Major Monogram (Cont.): "We've been using the information that you've gathered to replicate each and every one of Dr. Doofenshmirtz's inators."

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:37.900
And this, is where OWCA's motives finally become clear..

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:41.620
Dr. Doofenshmirtz may have been a terrible secret agent and bad villain

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:47.180
I mean bad as in incompetent of being a villain, not that he's a bad villain because, he's really kinda harm...

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:49.920
But he's a brilliant inventor

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:55.480
The fact that all his plans go sideways has less to do with the invention's themselves and more to do with the way he tries to use them

00:07:55.480 --> 00:08:00.900
Doofenshmirtz: "Hey all of my inators work, it's just that, ya know I don't use them properly. I have, poor planning skills.."

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:08.100
The auto-scan replication device in Perry's hat allows OWCA to benifit from Dr. Doofenshmirtz inventions,

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:12.420
without having to deal with the problems that he would cause them by being an agent

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:16.820
And the best part is, Doofenshmirtz is the one paying to construction them all.

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:19.520
Or, to be more accurate his ex wife is paying for it all.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:22.300
Doofenshmirtz: "I get a big alimony check every month so money is no object."

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:28.480
Doofenshmirtz evil incorporated is unwittingly serving as OWCA's research and development department.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:33.420
True, the do have to employ Perry to swoop in once a day to scan Doofenshmirtz 's latest inevntion,

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:36.600
And foil whatever evil plan he's trying to enact,

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:38.960
But that's way cheaper then funding the cost of their own R&amp;D

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:43.500
They let him run free so that they can continue to profit off of his work

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.100
And think about what Major Monogram said before

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:49.300
Major Monogram: "You've done more harm inside the agency then you ever did outside

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:52.800
If Doofenshmirtz is gonna be more of a hindrance then a help to whichever side he's on,

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:57.560
Then having him on the side of evil is actually the best possible outcome for OWCA.

00:08:57.560 --> 00:09:03.680
We know that Doofenshmirtz is a member of the League Of Villainous Evildoers Maniacally United For Frightening Investments in Naughtiness

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:06.240
(I don't know this guy's name, oops): "You want us to be called, love muffin?"

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:09.780
And Love Muffin does have some members who re actually dangerous criminals...

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:11.340
Like Reodenshtien.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:18.920
Reodenshtien: "I prefer you use my full name Aloyse Everheart Elizabeth Otto Wolfgang Hypatia Gunther Galen Gary Cooper von Roddenstein ."

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:22.500
Who plans to destroy summer forever by moving the earth away from the sun.

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:24.040
That's pretty evil.

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:29.700
And notice that at the end of the episode, Reodenshtien gets arrested, but doof? He's allowed to run free!

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:37.140
As we know form Major Monogram daily briefings with Perry, OWCA is always watching Doofenshmirtz's movements vigilantly.

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:40.160
Which means that wherever he goes, Perry can follow.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:44.580
Discovering where the evil guys are headed and what their next plan is

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:49.260
For so long, ten years now, we've been lead to believe that Doof is the bad guy

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:53.700
Something that even he seems to believe when he brands his company "Doofenshmirtz Evil incorporated."

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:58.480
Yet all of the evidence points to him actually being a tragic hero of Phineas and Ferb.

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:04.180
A hero who's contributions will never be known or appreciated outside of the OWCA.

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:07.140
Not even by Dr. Heniz Doofenshmirtz himself.

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:13.840
He's so deep undercover that not even realizes that all of his schemes are ultimately  helping the OWCA.

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:17.040
Both by acting as their research and development department,

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:24.120
And by inadvertently acting as the mole who lets them catch the more dangerous villains who actually pose a threat to the public.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:27.060
He may not have been the partner Perry the Platypus wanted,

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:30.820
But he turns out to be the nemesis that Perry needs.

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:36.020
But hey! That's just a theory! A Film Theory!

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:49.160
♫ *some boppin copyright free music* ♫ (definitely copyright free music)

